WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.034 --> 00:00:02.168
-You almost could not be here.

00:00:02.168 --> 00:00:03.336 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I almost didn´t make it
to the show tonight.

00:00:03.336 --> 00:00:04.604 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Because of jury duty.
-Yeah.

00:00:04.604 --> 00:00:06.339 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Light laughter ]
-That´s so fantastic.

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:08.875 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know,
I know that people say

00:00:08.875 --> 00:00:11.011 align:start size:94% position:6%
that they only get called once
every four years,

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:14.247 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I´m telling you --
I get called all of the time.

00:00:14.247 --> 00:00:16.182 align:start size:94% position:6%
They love me.
-I get it.

00:00:16.182 --> 00:00:17.717 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Light laughter ]
-They can´t get enough of me.

00:00:17.717 --> 00:00:20.553 align:start size:94% position:6%
I literally --
in the last four months,

00:00:20.553 --> 00:00:23.189 align:start size:94% position:6%
I have been asked to go
to petty court,

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:26.326 align:start size:94% position:6%
which I thought was petite...
[ Laughter ]

00:00:26.326 --> 00:00:28.028 align:start size:94% position:6%
...grand jury
and federal jury --

00:00:28.028 --> 00:00:30.130 align:start size:94% position:6%
or Supreme Court
and Federal Court.

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:32.799 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, my goodness.
-And I -- you know,

00:00:32.799 --> 00:00:36.136
when you get that thing
in the mail, everybody --

00:00:36.136 --> 00:00:37.837 size:88% position:44%
us New Yorkers are like,

00:00:37.837 --> 00:00:40.373
"My life is more important
than doing my civic duty."

00:00:40.373 --> 00:00:41.975 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, exactly.
-You know? I mean...

00:00:41.975 --> 00:00:43.777
And I´m actually civic-minded.

00:00:43.777 --> 00:00:46.479
I mean,
I actually pick up after my dog,

00:00:46.479 --> 00:00:48.448
and, you know, I don´t --

00:00:48.448 --> 00:00:50.717 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don´t jump
over the turnstiles.

00:00:50.717 --> 00:00:52.886 size:81% position:41%
And, you know, I vote.

00:00:52.886 --> 00:00:55.455 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, like, there´s something
so irritating about it.

00:00:55.455 --> 00:00:56.556 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-Yeah.

00:00:56.556 --> 00:00:58.224 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so,
you start to talk to people,

00:00:58.224 --> 00:01:00.460
and they´re like, "Oh, my God,
well, if you get to voir dire,"

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:01.928 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know --
-Sure.

00:01:01.928 --> 00:01:03.997
-That´s when they ask you
all these questions, like,

00:01:03.997 --> 00:01:05.632
"What´s your favorite --
Like, what´s your hobbies?"

00:01:05.632 --> 00:01:07.000 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean,
they ask you odd questions.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:08.835
But they -- they´re --
basically, you´re getting close

00:01:08.835 --> 00:01:11.404 align:start size:94% position:6%
to picked --
being picked for a jury.

00:01:11.404 --> 00:01:13.273 align:start size:94% position:6%
If you get there,
just start lying.

00:01:13.273 --> 00:01:14.908 align:start size:94% position:6%
And just say --
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:14.908 --> 00:01:16.376
Yeah, just start saying, like,

00:01:16.376 --> 00:01:18.678
"I don´t believe in the criminal
justice system as it is today."

00:01:18.678 --> 00:01:20.213 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:01:20.213 --> 00:01:23.149
-And, like, "I don´t think it´s
fair that people go to jail."

00:01:23.149 --> 00:01:24.884 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so you literally
start convincing yourself,

00:01:24.884 --> 00:01:26.052 size:75% position:38%
"I´m gonna say that.

00:01:26.052 --> 00:01:27.887 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like,
I´m actually gonna do that."

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:31.391 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then,
you walk in to the courtroom,

00:01:31.391 --> 00:01:33.460 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it looks like
a real courtroom

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:35.228 align:start size:94% position:6%
because it´s a real courtroom.
-Yeah.

00:01:35.228 --> 00:01:36.296 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:36.296 --> 00:01:39.099 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And --
And then a judge comes out.

00:01:39.099 --> 00:01:41.668
And he looks like a real judge.
-Yeah.

00:01:41.668 --> 00:01:43.736 size:84% position:42%
-Like, he´s not like
the "Law &amp; Order" judge

00:01:43.736 --> 00:01:45.138 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you thought.
-[ Chuckling ] Yeah.

00:01:45.138 --> 00:01:49.109
-And suddenly, you´re like,
"I can´t lie! I can´t lie."

00:01:49.109 --> 00:01:50.777
And they make you take the oath.
-Yeah.

00:01:50.777 --> 00:01:55.415
-And -- And he talks about
solemnizing the proceedings,

00:01:55.415 --> 00:01:57.183 align:start size:94% position:6%
which, I´ve never heard used
in that context.

00:01:57.183 --> 00:01:59.786 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you´re like,
"I swear to take -- to tell

00:01:59.786 --> 00:02:01.221 align:start size:94% position:6%
the whole truth
and nothing but the truth."

00:02:01.221 --> 00:02:03.790
And -- And you´re literally
thinking, "I´m gonna lie."

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:06.059
And then -- And then you
start to get, like, weepy,

00:02:06.059 --> 00:02:08.128
´cause you´re like, "Oh, my God,
the defendant is there.

00:02:08.128 --> 00:02:09.996 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he really counts on me,
you know..."

00:02:09.996 --> 00:02:12.198 align:start size:94% position:6%
-By the way --
-"...to show up."

00:02:12.198 --> 00:02:14.300 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And you´re surprised
they keep bringing you back?

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:16.302 align:start size:94% position:6%
You´re a dream juror.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:16.302 --> 00:02:18.505 align:start size:94% position:6%
You´re the dream --
everything about this!

00:02:18.505 --> 00:02:19.772 align:start size:94% position:6%
They´re like,
"Well, that lady --

00:02:19.772 --> 00:02:21.207 align:start size:94% position:6%
There was that one lady
who cried..."

00:02:21.207 --> 00:02:22.609 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:22.609 --> 00:02:24.744
"...when the judge stood up
and made everybody take an oath.

00:02:24.744 --> 00:02:26.513 align:start size:94% position:6%
We got to get her back here."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:26.513 --> 00:02:27.947 align:start size:94% position:6%
I´m sure everybody else
was on their phone,

00:02:27.947 --> 00:02:30.550 align:start size:94% position:6%
lying about everything,
saying, like,

00:02:30.550 --> 00:02:32.685
"I think like, shoplifting
should be the death penalty."

00:02:32.685 --> 00:02:34.087
They´re like, "Get out of here.

00:02:34.087 --> 00:02:36.856
We´ve got Kyra Sedgwick.
We don´t need you, you lunatic."

00:02:36.856 --> 00:02:38.858 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Light laughter ]
-Yeah, too much empathy.

00:02:38.858 --> 00:02:40.527 align:start size:94% position:6%
I´ve definitely -- Yeah.
-Too much empathy.

00:02:40.527 --> 00:02:41.861
Well, I want to talk to you
about -- well, this is empathy,

00:02:41.861 --> 00:02:43.530 align:start size:94% position:6%
but you care a lot
about thoughts and feelings.

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:44.797 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.

00:02:44.797 --> 00:02:46.432
-But are you coming
to a realization about this now,

00:02:46.432 --> 00:02:48.201
or you must have always cared
about thoughts and feelings.

00:02:48.201 --> 00:02:50.170
´Cause you strike me as someone
who´s always cared about --

00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:52.038 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, I´ve always cared
about thoughts and feelings.

00:02:52.038 --> 00:02:53.640 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-I mean, like, it´s a --

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:56.476
I literally had -- When my --
you know, my kids were little,

00:02:56.476 --> 00:02:57.377 align:start size:94% position:6%
I´d be like,
"Well, what are you feeling?

00:02:57.377 --> 00:02:58.811
Well, what are you thinking?

00:02:58.811 --> 00:03:00.280
Well, what are you feeling?
Well, what are you thinking?"

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:02.982
We literally had a game
called "Thoughts and Feelings,"

00:03:02.982 --> 00:03:04.517 size:84% position:42%
and they would hide it,

00:03:04.517 --> 00:03:06.186
´cause they didn´t want to play
the Thoughts and Feelings game.

00:03:06.186 --> 00:03:07.654 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Was it a --
Was it a board game?

00:03:07.654 --> 00:03:08.988 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was a board game.
-Oh, my God.

00:03:08.988 --> 00:03:10.790 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It made you talk
about thoughts and feelings.

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:12.592 size:81% position:41%
But, you know, I mean,

00:03:12.592 --> 00:03:14.928
this is the great thing
about having girlfriends,

00:03:14.928 --> 00:03:16.329 size:84% position:42%
is that they never tire

00:03:16.329 --> 00:03:17.463 align:start size:94% position:6%
of talking
about thoughts and feelings.

00:03:17.463 --> 00:03:18.498 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:18.498 --> 00:03:19.599 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Never.

00:03:19.599 --> 00:03:21.834 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, I mean,
no detail is too small.

00:03:21.834 --> 00:03:25.605 align:start size:94% position:6%
No emotion
is too minor to share,

00:03:25.605 --> 00:03:28.775 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, in deep, in depth,
in detail.

00:03:28.775 --> 00:03:30.643 align:start size:94% position:6%
The other day, I was having
dinner with my friend.

00:03:30.643 --> 00:03:32.145 size:78% position:39%
We were at two hours.

00:03:32.145 --> 00:03:34.180 align:start size:94% position:6%
And like, I´m asking her
everything about everything.

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:35.882 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, "What did you have
for breakfast?

00:03:35.882 --> 00:03:37.250 size:78% position:39%
And what did you wear

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:40.053
the day you went in to see your
boss and ask for a raise?

00:03:40.053 --> 00:03:41.454 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, how did you feel
in the morning?"

00:03:41.454 --> 00:03:42.522 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:42.522 --> 00:03:44.023 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like,
"Tell me every single thing."

00:03:44.023 --> 00:03:46.359 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we went
to the bathroom together,

00:03:46.359 --> 00:03:47.627 align:start size:94% position:6%
because women
go to the bathroom together.

00:03:47.627 --> 00:03:49.262
-This is something that --
-I´ve noticed that, yeah.

00:03:49.262 --> 00:03:51.631 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. This is something
that men don´t do.

00:03:51.631 --> 00:03:54.133 align:start size:94% position:6%
But we went
into the bathroom together.

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:58.104
Plenty of stalls, but we had to
go into the stall together.

00:03:58.104 --> 00:03:59.272 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Really?

00:03:59.272 --> 00:04:01.274 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Didn´t want to miss a nuance,
you know?

00:04:01.274 --> 00:04:03.042 align:start size:94% position:6%
Didn´t want to miss a --
you know, a --

00:04:03.042 --> 00:04:05.144 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You -- I excuse you
from jury duty.

00:04:05.144 --> 00:04:08.248 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:08.248 --> 00:04:11.017
So, you go into the stall
together, just to keep chatting?

00:04:11.017 --> 00:04:13.019
-Yeah, to keep chatting.
You don´t want to miss anything.

00:04:13.019 --> 00:04:15.521 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, like, talking over
the stall is not good enough.

00:04:15.521 --> 00:04:17.056 align:start size:94% position:6%
I need to see the face.
I need to --

00:04:17.056 --> 00:04:18.157 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Wow.

00:04:18.157 --> 00:04:19.425 size:81% position:41%
Are you concerned that

00:04:19.425 --> 00:04:20.526 align:start size:94% position:6%
other people in the bathroom
are aware...

00:04:20.526 --> 00:04:21.761 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No.

00:04:21.761 --> 00:04:22.795
-...that there are now
two people chatting away?

00:04:22.795 --> 00:04:23.997 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No.
-Okay. That´s great.

00:04:23.997 --> 00:04:25.164 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I don´t worry
about those things.

00:04:25.164 --> 00:04:26.966 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, no --
-I told Kev that story.

00:04:26.966 --> 00:04:30.903
He´s like, "You know, you can --
I can guaran-damn-tee it

00:04:30.903 --> 00:04:34.607
that no guy goes into a urinal,
like, you know,

00:04:34.607 --> 00:04:36.676 align:start size:94% position:6%
and has some guy right next
to him talking to him,

00:04:36.676 --> 00:04:38.077
because they can´t be apart."

00:04:38.077 --> 00:04:39.712
I mean, of course, they´re --
-I think that´s very safe.

00:04:39.712 --> 00:04:40.813 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, yeah.

00:04:40.813 --> 00:04:42.382 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I will say,

00:04:42.382 --> 00:04:44.851 align:start size:94% position:6%
´cause I recently saw you
and your husband, Kevin Bacon,

00:04:44.851 --> 00:04:47.020 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you are the best-looking
couple in show business.

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:49.188 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, my God, no.
-And if there was anyone --

00:04:49.188 --> 00:04:53.359 size:84% position:42%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:53.359 --> 00:04:55.928 align:start size:94% position:6%
If there was any guy
I would share a stall with,

00:04:55.928 --> 00:04:56.996 align:start size:94% position:6%
it would be your husband.
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:56.996 --> 00:04:57.997 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So...
[ Light laughter ]

00:04:57.997 --> 00:04:58.965
-You´re not the only one.

00:04:58.965 --> 00:05:00.166 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, no,
I´m sure there´s like --

00:05:00.166 --> 00:05:02.035 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Many a time, he´s had his...
in his hand...

00:05:02.035 --> 00:05:03.102 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Yeah.

00:05:03.102 --> 00:05:04.103 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...and people have asked
for autographs...

00:05:04.103 --> 00:05:05.571 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:05.571 --> 00:05:07.473 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...and pictures, selfies.
-Wow.

00:05:07.473 --> 00:05:09.842 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Just really easy. Just...
-Yeah, exactly.

00:05:09.842 --> 00:05:10.943 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

